1
00:00:00,740 --> 00:00:01,400
Right—keep it tidy.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:05,940
No, actually, don’t.

3
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:13,540
I bought a velvet waistcoat from a man called Dave,

4
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:16,180
He said, “It’s nearly vintage,” I said, “Nearly’s brave.”

5
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:18,860
Got a spreadsheet for my feelings, colour-coded in despair,

6
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:20,660
And a tiny little whistle for emergencies involving stairs.

7
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:23,920
I’m remarkably composed in a queue for a kebab,

8
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:26,420
Till a pigeon stole my napkin and I called it a cab.

9
00:00:26,460 --> 00:00:28,900
I’ve got manners like a butler, taste buds like a bin,

10
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:31,560
Put a crown upon a sausage and I’ll probably let it in.

11
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:32,340
Hold up—

12
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:33,000
What was that?

13
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:34,120
No, leave it.

14
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:35,980
That’s definitely part of the plan.

15
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:38,740
We’re doing fine, we’re doing fine,

16
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:41,220
Absolutely normal, every single time.

17
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:43,600
Hands up high if your life’s off-line,

18
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,300
We’re doing fine, we’re doing fine.

19
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:47,900
Say, “Fine!”

20
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:48,820
(Fine!)

21
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:50,480
Say, “Fine!”

22
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:50,780
(Fine!)

23
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:54,830
That’s the spirit—statistically, we’re fine.

24
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:59,020
I rehearsed an apology in case I bump a chair,

25
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:01,500
Then I blamed the architecture with a confident stare.

26
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:04,040
My neighbour owns a parrot that has learned to swear,

27
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:07,060
Now it’s more emotionally available than anyone upstairs.

28
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:09,800
I made a five-year plan, it lasted till Tuesday,

29
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:12,580
Bought a motivational mug, it said, “Try again someday.”

30
00:01:12,620 --> 00:01:14,920
My barber asked for guidance; I said, “Surprise me, mate,”

31
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:17,580
Now I look like a haunted pear that’s running late.

32
00:01:17,620 --> 00:01:19,020
The bass drops out—

33
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:20,000
The room gets tense—

34
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:21,190
I’ve got one thought

35
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:22,760
And it’s making no sense.

36
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:24,600
I’m fluent in excuses, conversational in cheek,

37
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:26,620
I can turn a minor setback to a documentary critique.

38
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:30,300
Got a sandwich in my pocket and a theory in my shoe,

39
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:32,820
If confidence was currency, I’d owe a pound or two.

40
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:34,560
You can call me unrealistic; I prefer “future-famous,”

41
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:38,020
I put “enigmatic” on a form that asked for “name and address.”

42
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:40,500
When the punchline lands sideways, let the brass section shout,

43
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:42,320
If you didn’t get the first one, there’s another one—watch out.

44
00:01:43,660 --> 00:01:46,300
We’re doing fine, we’re doing fine,

45
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:48,920
Absolutely normal, every single time.

46
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:51,340
Hands up high if your life’s off-line,

47
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:53,800
We’re doing fine, we’re doing fine.

48
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:55,520
Say, “Fine!”

49
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:56,500
(Fine!)

50
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:57,800
Say, “Fine!”

51
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:58,980
(Fine!)

52
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:03,000
That’s the spirit—statistically, we’re fine.

53
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:05,860
No further questions.

54
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:09,000
Please form an orderly panic.

55
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:13,000
We’re doing fine.
